&=\sum_{j=i}^\infty\left(\frac{(-1)^j}{2(j+1)}-\frac{(-1)^j}{2(j+3)}\right) \\
&=\frac{(-1)^i}{2(i+1)}+\frac{(-1)^{i+1}}{2(i+2)}-\frac{(-1)^i}{2(i+3)}-\frac{(-1)^{i+2}}{2(i+4)}+\cdots.
\end{align*}

We can now solve for the outer sum, using some properties of geometric series:

